# Test: SIGHUP reload of a plugin-only config, with no change.
# The daemon starts from a config whose only top-level block is `plugin { }`,
# receives SIGHUP, reloads (nothing changed), then receives SIGTERM.
# Expected: clean reload, the completion line, exit 0.
#
# This ran against the standalone hub orchestrator until 2026-08-12. That second
# runtime is deleted: a plugin-only config now boots the one daemon like every
# other config, and its SIGHUP goes through handleSIGHUPReload
# (cmd/ze/hub/main_reload.go). The reload is what is under test, so only the
# runtime under it changed.
#
# VALIDATES: a plugin-only config reloads on SIGHUP without restarting.
# PREVENTS: the plugin-only shape losing reload coverage with the orchestrator.

# Native trigger sends signals to the daemon.

# Plugin-only config: no bgp, no interface, no protocol block.
tmpfs=plugin-only.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture reload/reload-plugin-only-no-change-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze start plugin-only.conf:timeout=10s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=reloading config
# handleSIGHUPReload's stable completion line. Without it the daemon's last word
# is "reloading config..." whether the reload finished or wedged.
expect=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete
reject=stderr:pattern=reload error
